        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=3.5$",
          "worked": "The widths of A and B are $6+x$ and $15.5+x$. Their areas are equal.\n$$\\begin{align*}10(6+x)&=5(15.5+x)\\\\60+10x&=77.5+5x\\\\60+5x&=77.5\\\\5x&=17.5\\\\x&=3.5\\end{align*}$$\nCheck:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Area of A}&=10(6+3.5)=95\\\\\\text{Area of B}&=5(15.5+3.5)=95\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 50
      },
      {
        "id": "p96-q27-b",
